{start_of_verse: Verses 1}
Oh, my [G]golden slippers am laid away
‘Cause I don’t expect to wear ’em til my [D]wedding day
And my [D]long tailed coat, that I love so well
I will wear up in the chariot in the [G]morning
And my [G]long white robe that I bought last June
I’m goin’ to get changed ’cause it [D]fits too soon
And the [D]old grey hoss that I used to drive
I will hitch him to the chariot in the [G]morning
{end_of_verse}

