{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Oh, [G]my old banjo hangs on the wall
‘Cause it ain’t been tuned since [D]way last fall
But the [D]folks all say we’ll have a good time
When we ride up in the chariot in the [G]morning
There’s [G]ol’ brother Ben and his sister, Luce
They will telegraph the news to uncle [D]Bacco Juice
What a [D]great camp meetin’ there will be that day
When we ride up in the chariot in the [G]morning
{end_of_verse}

